  "comments": "A few main groups are known, which differ by thickness of all details. Most noticeably differences are visible on reverse, where in addition the type <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">E</span> has new spelling in Arabic.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reverse</span><br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> - the first alif &#039;ا&#039; in &#039;إسرائيل&#039; higher than corner.<br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> - the first alif &#039;ا&#039; in &#039;إسرائيل&#039; lower than corner, all details thick.<br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">C</span> - the first alif &#039;ا&#039; in &#039;إسرائيل&#039; lower than corner, all details thinner.<br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">D</span> - the first alif &#039;ا&#039; in &#039;إسرائيل&#039; to corner.<br />\r\nType <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">E</span> - the first alif &#039;ا&#039; with hamza &#039;ء&#039; in &#039;إسرائيل&#039; and points to corner.<br />\r\nPicture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/61bf0be721256.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/61bf0be721256.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"157\" height=\"250\" /></a><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Note</span>. There are many other differences between groups, these are marks for easy attribution.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Combinations</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span>: 5750.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>: 5751, 5752, 5754, 5755, 5757-5760.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> edge rounded: 5762.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">C</span> edge rounded: 5757, 5759.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">D</span>: 5765, 5766, 5768.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">E</span>: 5769-5777.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Note</span>. Dies of Obv. show similar changes in thickness of details, which are considered as non-essential.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">5757</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>, edge 12-sided, mint: Vantaa.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">C</span>, edge rounded 12-sided, mint: Utrecht.<br />\r\nPicture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/61cb905d23565.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/61cb905d23565.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"154\" /></a>",
